## Dining car

::bg{location="dining_car" time="night"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: The dining car smells of coffee kept hot too long. Crane has herded everyone in here. Nobody is eating.
@narrator{code="0020" when="!visited('car.dining')"}: Lise Varo sits at the piano with the lid down. Mirela Dace has a table to herself under a lamp that was never relit. Dr. Solt reads yesterday's paper with great attention.

<hub id="look" prompt="Where do you look?">
  <choice id="piano" text="The piano" once>
    @narrator{code="0030"}: Sheet music for "The Lamplighter's Daughter", the corners soft with use. Pencilled over the second verse, in a hurried hand: again.
  </choice>
  <choice id="table" text="Miss Dace's table" once>
    @narrator{code="0040"}: A cold cup, a crumpled napkin, a lamp with a black-sooted chimney. From here the piano is six feet away. Nobody at this table could have left it in the dark without walking into the singer.
  </choice>
  <choice id="steward" text="Ask the steward about the doctor" when="holds('empty', ['cab5', 'tunnel'])" once>
    @inspector{code="0010"}: Mr. Crane thought the doctor came through for a brandy during the tunnel.
    @steward{code="0010"}: Not through here, ma'am. I had the only lit match in the car, for the singer's music. I'd have seen a doctor.
    @inspector{code="0020" mono}: So the berth was empty and the dining car was empty of him too. Which leaves the corridor.
  </choice>
  <choice id="leave" text="Leave the car" exit>
    @narrator{code="0050"}: The door to the corridor sighs shut behind you.
  </choice>
</hub>
